{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA + implementation evidence (docs-only Verify)\\n\\nProblem: Gerrit Verify scheduled the full build/test OS×Python matrix plus mutation, packaging, optionality, artifact, eval, golden-path, and identity jobs for every patchset because gerrit-verify.yaml had no changed-path routing seam. A pure documentation change therefore consumed the same runners and wall clock as executable changes.\\n\\nProven mechanism: the workflow's unconditional job graph was the changeable artifact. A held-out workflow oracle failed before repair with \"Gerrit Verify has no trusted route-classification job\". The background fixer added a trusted-main classifier and reduced lane. Independent review then found three incomplete-coverage mechanisms: (1) make lint's check_dco_identity.py and check_criteria_vocabulary.py documentation guards were absent from the reduced lane; (2) conflict-marker and added-large-file hooks relevant to prose/images were absent; (3) target-branch workflow definitions can reference the extracted local composite action while an older open patchset's tree predates that action. Each was observed RED before repair through held-out or structural tests. The final action runs those reduced-only guards and a conservative docs-contract pytest selection; both workflows materialize trusted main's action only when the checked-out patchset lacks it.\\n\\nOSS comparison (current upstream main branches, researched 2026-08-14):\\n- CPython .github/workflows/reusable-context.yml + Tools/build/compute-changes.py compute run-docs/run-tests outputs, skip regular tests for Doc/Misc/documentation suffixes, retain docs and C-API-doc checks, and run full tests for non-doc paths.\\n- astral-sh/ruff .github/workflows/ci.yaml has a determine_changes job; docs/** and assets/** alone set code=false, expensive Rust/test jobs require code=true, and the mkdocs job remains required. Ruff explicitly warns that not every Markdown file is documentary because some Markdown files are tests.\\n- Django tests.yml uses paths-ignore: docs/** while docs.yml is selected by docs/** and performs a dedicated docs build.\\n- pandas unit-tests.yml ignores doc/** and web/**, while docbuild-and-upload.yml owns documentation/website validation.\\n- FastAPI uses a paths-filter classifier for test and docs jobs; its docs-affecting set conservatively includes pyproject.toml, uv.lock, workflow files, and scripts/docs.py, matching this ticket's decision that configuration, locks, workflows/actions, and scripts route to full Verify.\\n\\nThis is OSS consensus: change-aware test routing plus a dedicated documentation validation lane, with config/build inputs treated as executable impact. The rebar implementation is intentionally stricter than native paths-ignore because Gerrit workflow_dispatch requires the classifier and complete allowlist to execute from trusted origin/main, and every uncertainty routes full.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- Held-out oracle: RED before classifier; GREEN after repair; exact missing DCO guard mutation returned RED; restored GREEN.\\n- Older-patchset/action-skew oracle: RED without trusted-main fallback; GREEN after fallback.\\n- Conservative docs contract selection: 2,417 passed, 15 skipped in 114.15s locally (non-integration/non-external; roughly 80% of the default suite skipped).\\n- Direct documentation guards: ADR number/cross-reference, ADR index, env registry, docs index/dead links, README quickstart, CLI reference, MCP reference, DCO identity, and criteria vocabulary all passed.\\n- Pre-commit docs hygiene: merge-conflict and added-large-file hooks passed.\\n- Focused classifier/workflow/structural suite: 338 passed.\\n- make lint, actionlint, YAML validation, make typecheck (540 files), and git diff --check passed.\\n- No new dependency and no weakened test; full-route coverage/jobs remain intact and gain no additional docs runner job."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786727396086382001,"uuid":"63c7b97e-7a22-45fb-967c-18c6944a8c5e"}